<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[117, 67, 835, 107]]<|/det|>
group was removed via \(30\mathrm{min}\) agitation with \(20\%\) piperidine in DMF followed by filtration and washing.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 112, 888, 226]]<|/det|>
[596] Subsequent amino acids were coupled using Fmoc- protected amino acid (3.00 equiv), HBTU (2.85 equiv) and DIEA (6.00 equiv) in dry DMF, shaking for \(30\mathrm{min}\) . Pre- activation of any amino acid was not performed prior to coupling. Between amino acid couplings, the Fmoc protecting group was removed via \(30\mathrm{min}\) agitation with \(20\%\) piperidine in DMF followed by filtration and washing. Success of Fmoc removal steps and amino acid couplings were monitored qualitatively using a ninhydrin test.  

