<|ref|>sub_title<|/ref|><|det|>[[118, 388, 357, 405]]<|/det|>
## Example C1. Plasma Stability  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[116, 411, 881, 475]]<|/det|>
[739] The pooled frozen CD- 1 (ICR) mouse plasma was thawed in a water bath at \(37^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) prior to experiment. Plasma was centrifuged at \(4000\mathrm{rpm}\) for \(5\mathrm{min}\) and the clots were removed if any. pH was adjusted to \(7.4\pm 0.1\) if required.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 480, 891, 657]]<|/det|>
[740] Plasma ( \(98\mu \mathrm{L}\) ) and test compounds ( \(2\mu \mathrm{L}\) , \(100\mu \mathrm{M}\) , in DMSO) or reference compound propantheline bromide ( \(2\mu \mathrm{L}\) , \(100\mu \mathrm{M}\) in \(40\%\) v/v \(\mathrm{MeOH / H_2O}\) ) were added to the individual wells of a 96- well microtiter plate in duplicate. The plate was incubated at \(37^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) . During the incubation, aliquots were withdrawn at 0, 10, 30, 60, 120, and 300 minutes. \(100\mu \mathrm{L}\) \(4\% \mathrm{H_3PO_4}\) and \(800\mu \mathrm{L}\) of stop solution ( \(200\mathrm{ng / mL}\) tolbutamide and \(200\mathrm{ng / mL}\) labetalol in \(100\% \mathrm{CH_3CN}\) ) were added to precipitate unwanted proteins. After mixing thoroughly, the quenched aliquots were centrifuged at \(4,000\mathrm{rpm}\) for \(20\mathrm{min}\) . Aliquots ( \(100\mu \mathrm{L}\) ) of supernatant were transferred to a new plate. The samples were shaken at \(800\mathrm{rpm}\) for \(10\mathrm{min}\) before performing LC- MS/MS analysis.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[116, 663, 890, 727]]<|/det|>
[741] The analytes were detected by a multiple reaction monitoring method using a SCIEX Triple Quad \(6500+\) system equipped with an ACQUITY UPLC HSS T3 column ( \(100\mathrm{\AA}\) , \(1.8\mu \mathrm{m}\) , \(2.1\mathrm{mm}\times 30\) mm). Mobile phase A: water with \(0.1\%\) formic acid; Mobile phase B: \(\mathrm{CH_3CN}\) with \(0.1\%\) formic acid.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[116, 732, 900, 772]]<|/det|>
[742] The \(\%\) remaining of test compound after incubation in plasma was calculated using the following equation:  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[116, 778, 881, 818]]<|/det|>
[743] \(\%\) Remaining \(= 100\mathrm{x}\) (PAR (t) / PAR(t0)), where PAR is the peak area ratio of analyte versus internal standard (IS)  

