<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 323, 901, 455]]<|/det|>
[744] The pharmacokinetics of peptide are determined using male CD- 1 (ICR) mice purchased from Vital River Laboratory Animal Co., Ltd., Beijing, China. All animal studies are conducted in accordance with the highest standards of care as outlined in the NIH Guide for Care and Use of Laboratory. Following injection of the mice ( \(10\mathrm{mg / kg}\) , 3 mice per test compound) with aliquots of the peptides in 10 mM PBS ( \(2\mathrm{mg / mL}\) , pH 7.4) via the tail vein, blood samples are collected into pre- chilled tubes containing Heparin- Na ( \(3\mu \mathrm{L}\) , \(1,000\mathrm{I.U / mL}\) ) at 5, 30, 60, and 240 min.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 459, 904, 612]]<|/det|>
[745] General sample processing procedure: An aliquot of \(12\mu \mathrm{L}\) diluted blood sample ( \(10\mathrm{x}\) dilution factor for 30, 60, and 240 min blood samples; \(20\mathrm{x}\) dilution factor for 5 min blood samples), calibration standard, dilution quality control, single blank or double blank samples are added to the individual wells of a low binding 96- well plate. Each sample (except the double blank) is quenched with \(120\mu \mathrm{L}\) MeOH. The resulting mixtures are mixed for 10 min at \(800\mathrm{rpm}\) and centrifuged at \(3,220\mathrm{g}\) ( \(4000\mathrm{rpm}\) ) for 15 min at \(4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) . Supernatant aliquots ( \(50\mu \mathrm{L}\) ) are transferred to a clean low binding 96- well plate and centrifuged at \(3,220\mathrm{g}\) ( \(4000\mathrm{rpm}\) ) for 5 min at \(4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) , then the samples are directly injected for LC- MS/MS analysis.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 617, 901, 749]]<|/det|>
[746] The analytes are detected by a multiple reaction monitoring method using a SCIEX Triple Quad \(6500+\) system equipped with an ACQUITY UPLC HSS T3 column ( \(100\mathrm{\AA}\) , \(1.8\mu \mathrm{m}\) , \(2.1\mathrm{mm}\times 30\mathrm{mm}\) ). Mobile phase A: water/CHCN ( \(95 / 5\) , v/v) with \(0.1\%\) formic acid and \(2\mathrm{mM}\) ammonium formate; Mobile phase B: CHCN/water ( \(95 / 5\) , v/v) with \(0.1\%\) formic acid and \(2\mathrm{mM}\) ammonium formate. Or Mobile phase A: water with \(0.1\%\) formic acid; Mobile phase B: CHCN with \(0.1\%\) formic acid. Column temperature: \(60^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) .  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[117, 754, 863, 819]]<|/det|>
[747] The plasma concentration- time data is subjected to IV- noncompartmental pharmacokinetics analysis using Phoenix WinNonlin (version 6.3, Pharsight Corp., Mountain View, CA, USA). The linear/log trapezoidal rule is applied in obtaining the PK parameters.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[117, 844, 905, 885]]<|/det|>
Example C3. In vitro determination of bound and unbound fraction of EphA2 binding constructs to human serum albumin (HSA).  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[117, 891, 845, 930]]<|/det|>
[748] HSA- HPLC method (measurement of drug protein binding by immobilized human serum albumin- HPLC).

<--- Page Split --->
<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 68, 895, 425]]<|/det|>
[749] A 13- min HPLC (Thermo Vanquish Horizon with Diode Array Detector) gradient method is used to determine the HSA (Human Serum Albumin) binding of novel compounds using a chemically bonded protein stationary phase (ChiralPAK HSA HPLC column, \(50 \times 4 \mathrm{mm}\) ). The HSA binding values are derived from the gradient retention times that are converted to the logarithm of the equilibrium constant using data from a calibration set of molecules. The \(\%\) bound to plasma values for the calibrator compounds are converted to the linear free energy values using the following equation: \(\mathrm{LogK} = \mathrm{log}[\% \mathrm{PPB} / (101 - \% \mathrm{PPB})]\) . The logarithmic value of the gradient retention times from the experiment are plotted against the linearized values of the \(\%\) bound to plasma. The slope and the intercept are used to convert the retention times to linear free energy values (LogK), from which the estimated \(\%\) protein binding is calculated using the following equation: \(\% \mathrm{Binding} = [(101 \cdot 10^{\mathrm{LogK}}) / (1 + 10^{\mathrm{LogK}})]\) . Aqueous mobile phase (mobile phase A) is \(50 \mathrm{mM}\) ammonium acetate solution, pH 7.4 and the organic mobile phase (mobile phase B) is 2- propanol. The flow rate is set at \(0.35 \mathrm{mL} / \mathrm{min}\) and injection volume was 5 \(\mu \mathrm{L}\) , with samples prepared at \(0.5 \mathrm{mg} / \mathrm{mL}\) concentration in 50:50 mobile phase. The initial LC conditions are set at \(0\%\) B and ramped to \(50\%\) B over 8.5 min, then held at \(50\%\) B for 1.5 min before going back to initial conditions and re- equilibrating the column for 2.5 min. Chromatograms are recorded at \(280 \mathrm{nm}\) by a diode array UV absorption detector.  

<|ref|>sub_title<|/ref|><|det|>[[118, 429, 729, 447]]<|/det|>
## Example C4. Protocol-FACS analysis for biotinylated compound cell binding  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[115, 451, 904, 695]]<|/det|>
[750] Cells were split, counted, and resuspended in cold PBS. Cells were stained with Zombie Violet dye (1:1000 in PBS) at dark for 15 min. Cells were washed two times with cold PBS by centrifugation ( \(\overline{a} 1,500 \mathrm{RPM}\) for 3 min). A total of \(50 \mathrm{K}\) cells per \(90 \mu \mathrm{L}\) cell culture media were seeded in each well of a 96 wells of U bottom plate. \(10 \mu \mathrm{L}\) of serial diluted compounds were added to \(90 \mu \mathrm{L}\) of cells in each well. For biotinylated compounds in direct binding experiments: 3- fold of serial diluted biotinylated compounds are prepared with DMSO in a separate plate prior to adding to cells. Cells were incubated with compounds on ice for 1 hour for binding. Cells were then washed 3 times with cold PBS by centrifugation ( \(\overline{a} 1,500 \mathrm{RPM}\) for 3 min). Compounds bound cells were then stained with Streptavidin- AF647 (1:2000 dilution in PBS) on ice for 30 minutes. Cells were washed 3 times with cold PBS by centrifugation ( \(\overline{a} 1,500 \mathrm{RPM}\) for 3 minutes). Cells were resuspended in \(100 \mu \mathrm{L}\) of cold PBS and proceeded to APC signal acquisition on CytoFlex.  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[117, 700, 886, 740]]<|/det|>
