## Example C8. Biodistribution Study  

<|ref|>text<|/ref|><|det|>[[117, 236, 901, 390]]<|/det|>
[761] Male athymic nude mice (Crown Bioscience) are inoculated with PC3 prostate cancer cells on their right shoulders. Animals \((n = 20)\) with tumor volume \(200 - 390 \mathrm{mm}^3\) are enrolled in the imaging study and categorized into three groups \((n = 4 / \mathrm{group})\) . Per group allocation, each subject is dosed intravenously (IV) with one \(^{177}\mathrm{Lu}\) - radiolabeled peptide \((100 - 120 \mu \mathrm{L}, \sim 1000 \mu \mathrm{Ci})\) and imaged using longitudinal multi- animal whole body single- photon emission computed tomography/computed tomography (SPECT/CT). Following the final imaging time point at \(48 \mathrm{h}\) post- radiotracer administration, all mice are euthanized, and tissues resected for ex vivo radioanalysis using gamma counter.  

